---
Headings: numeric
---

# Heading :label[a] @label[b]

The `@name[...]` inline and `@name+[...]` block forms share the begin-end
registry and coexist with the `:`/`::`/`:::` directives.

Cross-reference parity (`@` must resolve identically to `:`):
ref :ref[a] then @ref[b]; cref :cref[a] then @cref[b]; Cref :Cref[a] then @Cref[b]

Span parity: :span[hello] then @span[hello]

@note+[A block note set with the plus form.]

A paragraph after the block, with an inline @note[note] mid-sentence.

Generic unregistered names show the default flip — inline @thing[x] is a span,
while the block form is a div:

@thing+[block thing]
